WEBVTT

00:01.380 --> 00:02.690
In the present time,

00:03.400 --> 00:07.070
with VR headgear,
you can go into a virtual world

00:07.070 --> 00:10.410
and play as the resident of that world.

00:13.080 --> 00:17.540
VR Full-Dive games are
at the height of their popularity.

00:19.750 --> 00:22.920
And there exists

00:22.920 --> 00:27.170
a god-tier game that stands
above all other games

00:27.170 --> 00:29.130
with over thirty million
players worldwide.

00:31.140 --> 00:33.140
And the name of that game is...

00:40.020 --> 00:42.270
Shangri-La Frontier.

01:03.210 --> 01:09.130
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

02:18.490 --> 02:22.750
#31: DESPAIR AFTER THE ONSLAUGHT

02:23.710 --> 02:27.000
EIGHTHOLD

02:39.320 --> 02:44.760
I fought scorpions all night long,
so I'm kinda sleepy.

02:47.550 --> 02:50.650
Oh right, I wonder how Bilac's doing.

02:51.360 --> 02:53.650
Is she an Ancient Craftsman yet?

02:56.200 --> 03:02.660
She needs to be one to repair
a Non-Standard Ether Reactor, after all.

03:03.160 --> 03:05.370
You're right on time, Mr. Sunraku!

03:05.370 --> 03:07.670
Hey, Emul. Glad to see you.

03:08.210 --> 03:11.170
I thought I'd have to wait all day again.

03:11.630 --> 03:13.920
Can we go to Rabitz now?

03:13.920 --> 03:15.190
Yessir!

03:20.020 --> 03:21.680
All right!

03:26.730 --> 03:31.190
Mr. Sunraku, it feels like your Vorpal Soul
is ranging more than usual!

03:31.190 --> 03:33.360
Oh, you can tell?

03:35.240 --> 03:39.240
I bet you'll be shocked once
you hear what I accomplished.

03:44.450 --> 03:47.790
Wh-Whoa! Quit screaming
out of nowhere! You startled me!

03:47.790 --> 03:52.420
Y-Y-Y-You defeated a Goldy Scorpion?!

03:52.420 --> 03:53.710
That's amazing!

03:53.710 --> 03:56.720
You're like the embodiment of Vorpal Soul!

03:56.720 --> 03:59.680
T-This is Goldy Scorpion's

03:59.680 --> 03:59.970
Gleaming Crystal Stinger...

03:59.970 --> 04:01.140
GLEAMING CRYSTAL STINGER
Gleaming Crystal Stinger...

04:01.140 --> 04:02.850
GLEAMING CRYSTAL STINGER

04:02.850 --> 04:05.640
I never dreamed I'd see one
with my own eyes...

04:07.060 --> 04:09.100
There's more where that came from!

04:10.150 --> 04:12.190
Reaping Crystal Claw!

04:12.190 --> 04:13.730
Darkening Crystal Shell!

04:13.730 --> 04:15.110
Whipping Crystal Tail!

04:17.860 --> 04:19.530
And here's the coup de grace!

04:20.620 --> 04:23.870
Goldy Scorpion's Crystal Lifecore!

04:29.290 --> 04:33.420
You said you wanted Crystal Scorpion
parts to craft weapons with,

04:33.420 --> 04:35.280
but won't this do you better?

04:35.280 --> 04:37.880
You oughta craft something
more awesome with this, I bet!

04:38.880 --> 04:41.660
Mr. Sunraku, what's this?

04:42.330 --> 04:44.180
It's so pretty.

04:44.180 --> 04:47.100
That's Crystal Scorpion's excrement.

04:50.730 --> 04:54.360
I went through a lot after beating
the golden scorpion, you know?

04:56.640 --> 04:58.030
I'm not gonna die no matter what!

04:58.030 --> 05:02.660
After all, I had to go back to town
without using Inventoria.

05:05.160 --> 05:09.580
So, Bilac,
how's the Ancient Craftsman thing going?

05:09.580 --> 05:11.620
You said you wanted time.

05:13.040 --> 05:14.250
Bilac?

05:14.250 --> 05:16.130
What's wrong?

05:21.630 --> 05:24.220
S-She's dead!

05:26.140 --> 05:27.890
Oh, no!

05:27.890 --> 05:31.640
After all the hard work
I did to raise her!

05:32.270 --> 05:33.650
You'll be deeply mi—

05:34.650 --> 05:37.820
Don't go killin' me off, ya dimwit!

05:40.920 --> 05:43.700
But really, you knocked
my socks off with this one.

05:43.700 --> 05:46.660
Mr. Sunraku, are you okay?!

05:48.370 --> 05:52.170
And no need to worry,
I'm already an Ancient Craftsman.

05:53.450 --> 05:57.460
Now I can handle Divinity-era stuff.

05:58.050 --> 06:00.510
And the thing you wanted me to fix...

06:00.510 --> 06:02.720
NON-STANDARD ETHER REACTOR
Here, as you can see!

06:02.720 --> 06:06.260
Whoa! A functioning
Non-Standard Ether Reactor!

06:06.260 --> 06:08.640
You completely fixed it!

06:09.970 --> 06:13.770
Just as I expect from you, Bilac!
You really did it!

06:13.770 --> 06:15.230
Hey, put me down!

06:15.230 --> 06:17.420
I knew you could do it, Sis Bee!

06:24.740 --> 06:26.820
My fatigue's all gone now!

06:26.820 --> 06:30.950
With this, I should be able
to use those Legacy Weapons!

06:31.330 --> 06:35.330
I'll go wild with those SF suits! Yeah!

06:35.330 --> 06:37.170
Yes, you will!

06:37.170 --> 06:38.960
SF suits?

06:38.960 --> 06:40.420
Yeah!

06:40.420 --> 06:46.340
Like the one I gave you, there were plenty
of other Legacy Weapons in Inventoria.

06:47.010 --> 06:49.350
And there were sets of armor called

06:49.350 --> 06:52.020
NON-STANDARD SPECIALIZED ARMOR
Non-Standard Specialized Armor required

06:52.020 --> 06:53.350
NON-STANDARD SPECIALIZED ARMOR
to wield those weapons!

06:53.350 --> 06:53.850
TACTICAL BEAST

06:53.850 --> 06:55.520
TACTICAL BEAST
I'm also looking forward

06:55.520 --> 06:56.850
TACTICAL BEAST
to testing out the Tactical Beasts,

06:56.850 --> 06:59.980
but the armor is what
I care about the most!

07:00.480 --> 07:03.250
So anyway, I'll see you guys later!

07:07.660 --> 07:09.520
He's so restless.

07:09.990 --> 07:12.040
SF suits, huh?

07:22.880 --> 07:26.180
Okay, which one should I test out first?

07:26.760 --> 07:29.680
Hmm, let's see...

07:29.680 --> 07:32.140
To turn on the powered suits,

07:32.140 --> 07:37.350
I have to set the reactor into
the corresponding Tactical Beast?

07:37.350 --> 07:38.690
Uh-huh.

07:39.520 --> 07:43.150
Okay, let's equip one right away!

07:43.150 --> 07:47.700
Equip one right away!

07:51.330 --> 07:52.990
Equip?

08:02.920 --> 08:04.880
He's back.

08:04.880 --> 08:06.300
That's rather quick.

08:10.970 --> 08:12.560
Mr. Sunraku?

08:12.930 --> 08:14.680
What's the matt—

08:18.560 --> 08:21.910
Because of the Lycagon's Mark...

08:22.520 --> 08:27.110
I can't equip a dang thing, dammit!

08:28.530 --> 08:32.410
Ya called it armor,
so I kinda had a hunch.

08:32.410 --> 08:38.040
They were full-body sets of armor,
so I thought some miracle could happen!

08:40.830 --> 08:46.380
CANNOT EQUIP

08:47.050 --> 08:49.510
I can't equip every single one of them...

08:49.510 --> 08:52.390
And what frustrates me the most...

08:52.750 --> 08:57.060
At this rate, those two scumbags
who barely did anything

08:57.060 --> 09:00.770
will get to have fun
with them before I can!

09:01.400 --> 09:04.520
Why won't things work out for me?!

09:04.520 --> 09:06.820
I'm about to have a mental breakdown!

09:06.820 --> 09:10.570
And I'm about to have
a cheek breakdown, too...

09:12.450 --> 09:14.120
Mr. Sunraku?

09:15.160 --> 09:16.870
Okay...

09:16.870 --> 09:18.620
I've made up my mind, Emul.

09:21.750 --> 09:25.000
I'll go into hiding.

09:25.000 --> 09:27.380
You can go off
and do your own thing for a while.

09:27.380 --> 09:28.630
What?!

09:28.630 --> 09:31.260
Without a Non-Standard Ether Reactor,

09:31.260 --> 09:34.970
those two wouldn't be able to use
any of the Legacy Weapons either!

09:34.970 --> 09:36.510
Eat that!

09:36.970 --> 09:39.100
Yer quite a scumbag yerself.

09:39.100 --> 09:42.230
Please come back real soon!

09:42.230 --> 09:44.480
Once my mental health
recovers enough, though.

09:44.480 --> 09:46.980
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

09:47.980 --> 09:50.990
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

10:17.300 --> 10:19.310
HIZUTOME

10:29.860 --> 10:33.990
Um, oh! Look at the time! I gotta go now!

10:40.950 --> 10:43.910
That being said, what to do now?

10:45.560 --> 10:48.630
I was so looking forward to it,
and that makes it hurt even more.

10:48.990 --> 10:51.460
What are you whining about so early?

10:51.460 --> 10:54.590
Ever since the summer break
started, no, even before that,

10:54.590 --> 10:57.180
you've been living the life
of a hopeless slacker.

10:57.180 --> 11:02.350
Hey, I'm enjoying life better than you
who wasted half of your youth working PT.

11:02.350 --> 11:07.940
As long as the other half
is shining bright, I'm happy enough!

11:08.730 --> 11:09.630
Rumi.

11:10.190 --> 11:15.360
Knowing half your brain's been infected
by positivity, I wanna ask you something.

11:15.860 --> 11:17.030
What is it?

11:17.460 --> 11:22.200
Let's say you saved up to buy
this outfit you really wanted...

11:22.200 --> 11:25.790
...only to discover that it's for babies.
What would you do?

11:25.790 --> 11:27.420
How is that even possible?

11:27.420 --> 11:29.130
It's just a metaphor.

11:29.540 --> 11:32.130
So basically, what to do
when you make a mistake, right?

11:32.130 --> 11:37.340
If it were me, I'd put on some other
outfit I like and just forget about it.

11:37.340 --> 11:40.100
But in my case,
I have no "other outfit"...

11:42.600 --> 11:45.100
I could actually do that!

11:45.560 --> 11:47.060
Aaah!

11:47.060 --> 11:50.440
You're a big help, Rumi.

11:50.940 --> 11:53.780
What're you gonna do about this?!
You ruined my clothes!

11:53.780 --> 11:56.860
Heh, why don't you put on
other clothes and just forget it?

11:56.860 --> 11:59.280
You dummy!

12:00.450 --> 12:03.700
Relieve the stress you got
from a game with another game.

12:03.700 --> 12:06.460
How could I forget
such an obvious thing?

12:07.750 --> 12:11.570
That means what I need is...

12:12.210 --> 12:13.210
NOT TRASH GAMES - ADDICTIVE TRASH GAMES

12:14.210 --> 12:15.300
NOT TRASH GAMES

12:15.300 --> 12:17.720
NOT TRASH GAMES
All right, I'll go with that.

12:18.100 --> 12:23.970
One of the few faves of mine
that aren't actually trashy.

12:24.970 --> 12:27.980
It's been a while since I booted you up.

12:27.980 --> 12:29.770
Nephilim Hollow.

12:33.270 --> 12:37.900
How long has it been?
Two... no, three months?

12:51.040 --> 12:52.840
NEPHILIM = MACHINE-CLAD MAN
"Nephilim Hollow."

12:52.840 --> 12:54.040
NEPHILIM = MACHINE-CLAD MAN
A robot action game

12:54.040 --> 12:55.800
where you can customize and fight

12:55.800 --> 12:59.050
with mechs that came down
from the sky called "Nephilim."

12:59.050 --> 13:00.550
SUNRAKU

13:00.550 --> 13:03.850
I'll work off the stress
I got from being denied

13:03.850 --> 13:07.350
wearing SF-powered suits
in SLF with this robot suit!

13:08.310 --> 13:11.440
Hey, it's been a while.
Let's get wild.

13:12.270 --> 13:13.690
Kingfisher.

13:40.130 --> 13:45.050
What was I doing the last time
I logged in here, anyway?

13:46.510 --> 13:49.180
Oh, right! I was going
all out on ranked matches

13:49.180 --> 13:52.270
'cuz I wanted to reach
the top of the online rank!

13:52.270 --> 13:57.900
I think I got matched with
the #1 Player and it ended in a tie.

13:57.900 --> 14:01.990
What was her name again?

14:03.410 --> 14:05.280
Is she still playing this game?

14:13.620 --> 14:18.420
That kettlehead and common
kingfisher-like default colors...

14:18.420 --> 14:19.880
Kingfisher!

14:21.010 --> 14:23.720
You're finally back, Sunraku!

14:23.720 --> 14:27.260
I, Super Ballman, will kick your ass
once and for all!

14:31.980 --> 14:32.980
SUPER BALLMAN CHALLENGED YOU TO A DUEL

14:32.980 --> 14:34.980
SUPER BALLMAN CHALLENGED YOU TO A DUEL
"Super Tama-O"?

14:35.360 --> 14:36.260
Who were you again?

14:36.260 --> 14:40.790
Hey! It's me, Super Ballman!
We fought in a ranked match before!

14:41.440 --> 14:43.740
Huh?! You seriously forgot about me?!

14:43.740 --> 14:45.990
I was acting like your archnemesis and all!

14:46.490 --> 14:49.580
That was, like, three months ago.

14:49.580 --> 14:52.540
If I don't remember it,
I must've wiped the floor with you.

14:53.960 --> 14:56.750
You goddamn rank wrecker!

14:56.750 --> 14:59.550
I'll make sure you regret forgetting me!

14:59.940 --> 15:01.920
Accept my challenge, Sunraku!

15:01.920 --> 15:04.550
Let me show you what
the #2 player can do!

15:12.060 --> 15:14.560
Wow, number two, eh?

15:15.060 --> 15:16.980
Not a bad match to get me back in shape.

15:23.570 --> 15:26.410
I'll smash you for good

15:26.410 --> 15:27.990
with my Bound Dog this time, Kingfisher!

15:27.990 --> 15:29.580
BOUND DOG - KINGFISHER
with my Bound Dog this time, Kingfisher!

15:29.580 --> 15:30.090
KINGFISHER VS BOUND DOG

15:30.090 --> 15:33.620
KINGFISHER VS BOUND DOG
Kingfisher VS Bound Dog!

15:34.000 --> 15:36.080
Duel Start!

15:37.790 --> 15:39.880
Let's get this started!

15:43.590 --> 15:48.680
The robots in this game, Nephilim,
aren't the type you control from the cockpit,

15:48.680 --> 15:53.060
but rather you quite literally
fight by fusing with it.

15:56.350 --> 15:59.730
My robot is geared towards speed
more than anything,

15:59.730 --> 16:02.400
it'd be fun to pair that up
with some massive firepower,

16:02.400 --> 16:06.110
resulting in one heck
of a silly dream-like unit.

16:06.900 --> 16:08.280
What a speed!

16:08.280 --> 16:12.410
But as a result, because I went
all out on making it fast,

16:12.410 --> 16:18.540
this Kingfisher could only hold out
for three minutes with its energy tank.

16:18.540 --> 16:23.960
In other words, if I can finish the match
in three minutes, I'm all good, but...

16:25.420 --> 16:27.800
Where are you aiming at, doofus?!

16:27.800 --> 16:29.050
I don't even have to dodge!

16:29.970 --> 16:33.930
Damn it! This thing's as difficult
to control as ever!

16:38.850 --> 16:44.070
Despite being a quality game,
this game only has a small player base.

16:44.070 --> 16:47.570
And the reason why I decided
to play this game...

16:48.040 --> 16:51.570
Unlike in other robot games where you
operate the robot with buttons or levers,

16:51.990 --> 16:55.120
here you use your own thoughts
to move not only your limbs

16:55.120 --> 16:59.580
but also every non-human body parts,
such as missiles and boosters.

16:59.580 --> 17:03.340
At the same time, you also need
to work your weapons and fight.

17:04.130 --> 17:07.340
All of those are enough to overheat
an average player's brain.

17:07.800 --> 17:11.720
Even more, if you're built for speed,
it's going to make you crazy.

17:11.720 --> 17:15.470
I couldn't turn well enough.
My feints were too simple.

17:15.470 --> 17:18.730
Can't believe I got this rusty
just from not playing for a bit.

17:18.730 --> 17:21.060
Don't you eat a lot of fuel?

17:21.060 --> 17:24.520
You ain't gonna beat me
if you just keep running, Sunraku!

17:24.520 --> 17:25.270
Heh!

17:26.400 --> 17:27.530
Flexible laser, huh?!

17:31.740 --> 17:34.740
Heh, looks like I'm getting
my muscle memory back.

17:34.740 --> 17:37.240
Kinda late for that, though!

17:37.240 --> 17:39.250
Panzer Puncher!

17:56.010 --> 18:00.500
Tch, so much for my flexible laser.

18:01.400 --> 18:05.520
Well played, Sunraku.
Making that strike in that situation...

18:06.650 --> 18:09.110
But I've destroyed your wings!

18:09.110 --> 18:11.610
You can't fly your way out of me anymore!

18:12.110 --> 18:15.030
Because of how Kingfisher was designed,

18:15.030 --> 18:19.620
if even one part is damaged,
it'll severely impact its mobility.

18:21.020 --> 18:24.370
Well, now what?

18:27.170 --> 18:31.880
Hey, c'mon! How long are you
gonna keep hiding in that rubble?!

18:31.880 --> 18:34.720
I'll blow you out with Panzer Puncher!

18:38.680 --> 18:41.810
You think you can hit me
by firing randomly?!

18:41.810 --> 18:43.980
You're out of options, Sunraku!

18:43.980 --> 18:46.690
I've been waiting for this
moment for three whole months!

18:46.690 --> 18:49.320
I can finally get my revenge on you!

18:52.360 --> 18:53.740
Not on my watch, you idiot!

18:54.110 --> 18:55.280
I won't let you...

18:55.280 --> 18:59.280
And that made you mistake
rubble for your foe.

19:00.680 --> 19:02.580
Greed's a scary thing, huh?

19:02.580 --> 19:07.040
Sunraku! Damn you!

19:11.000 --> 19:14.550
WINNER: KINGFISHER
Winner: Kingfisher!

19:14.550 --> 19:15.050
WINNER: KINGFISHER

19:24.560 --> 19:30.070
Yeah! That felt great!
The robot game is one hell of a blast!

19:30.070 --> 19:33.110
Hey! That wasn't fair!

19:33.110 --> 19:36.490
Oh, really? You simply fell for my plan.

19:37.660 --> 19:39.990
One more! I want a rematch!

19:39.990 --> 19:41.330
Uhh...

19:41.330 --> 19:44.830
I'm the man who'll beat Rust
and become the number one!

19:44.830 --> 19:47.080
I can't go around losing here!

19:47.080 --> 19:48.330
Rust?

19:49.290 --> 19:50.710
Oh, yeah.

19:52.820 --> 19:53.610
You...

19:56.260 --> 20:00.010
Done with the opening match?
It's my turn now.

20:00.640 --> 20:02.930
I finally remember.

20:02.930 --> 20:07.020
That robot, that avatar...
Long time no see.

20:07.420 --> 20:11.190
The player I could just
barely get a tie against...

20:11.190 --> 20:12.920
The number one in the rankings...

20:13.900 --> 20:15.120
Rust.

21:49.830 --> 21:52.750
SLF Theater!

21:52.750 --> 21:53.670
#34: WINDOW SHOPPING

21:53.670 --> 21:55.130
#34: WINDOW SHOPPING
Mini!

21:55.130 --> 21:56.250
#34: WINDOW SHOPPING

22:02.970 --> 22:05.600
That half-naked
bird-head is here again.

22:05.600 --> 22:08.060
Stop it, don't look him in the eye.

22:08.060 --> 22:10.390
Shh! He'll hear you.

22:10.390 --> 22:10.890
ARMOR SHOP

22:10.890 --> 22:13.100
ARMOR SHOP
He always comes here.

22:13.100 --> 22:15.980
ARMOR SHOP
Because of him, I couldn't shop in peace.

22:15.980 --> 22:19.860
Half-naked and those scars...
Are we sure he's not some criminal?

22:19.860 --> 22:22.070
Either that, or he's just a pervert.

22:22.070 --> 22:24.990
Well, he's a pervert either way.

22:24.990 --> 22:26.950
I thought that too, actually.

22:26.950 --> 22:29.290
Yeah, he's a pervert.

22:29.290 --> 22:32.330
Don't look him in the eye,
or else he'll take your clothes off.

22:32.330 --> 22:36.210
If he shows up, just start running
and don't look back!

22:36.210 --> 22:38.710
What is that pervert, a monster?!

22:42.840 --> 22:45.720
JUST A GUY WHO CAN'T EQUIP ANYTHING
ON HIS TORSO AND LEGS

22:45.720 --> 22:49.310
BECAUSE OF LYCAGON'S CURSE
Maybe I should curse them for real...

22:54.100 --> 22:57.150
SLF Theater!

22:57.150 --> 22:57.940
#35: SUPER MODEL TOWA AMANE

22:57.940 --> 22:59.360
#35: SUPER MODEL TOWA AMANE
Mini!

22:59.360 --> 23:00.570
#35: SUPER MODEL TOWA AMANE

23:01.190 --> 23:02.650
What's this?

23:02.650 --> 23:04.320
Towa Amane's specialty;

23:04.320 --> 23:06.740
"When someone took a picture of her
without warning,

23:06.740 --> 23:09.120
even though she couldn't
have noticed the camera,

23:09.120 --> 23:11.660
she's able to strike a perfect pose."

23:12.370 --> 23:13.960
Are you serious?

23:15.830 --> 23:18.040
Thanks very much!

23:22.800 --> 23:23.920
Seriously?

23:35.060 --> 23:36.310
Seriously?

23:38.810 --> 23:40.690
JAPAN'S HIGHEST PEAK MT. FUJI

23:45.400 --> 23:49.820
Then how about with this super
telephoto from a 50km distance?!

23:52.660 --> 23:53.690
Seriously?
